0..75 Comment "// The circle\'s loop space, presented at the term stratum: `Loop(x)` is \"x,"
76..145 Comment "// then the loop\" and `Unloop(x)` \"x, then its inverse\", with the two"
146..220 Comment "// cancellations as rules, so these terms are, one stratum down, the words"
221..300 Comment "// that `Path[.A = Circle](Base, Base)` is in `circle.gandr`, the book\'s circle"
301..379 Comment "// (§ 8.1). Conversion reads a word by its normal form, and a fold out of the"
380..457 Comment "// words is admitted only when it respects both rules, as the mirror does and"
458..533 Comment "// a case that tells a loop from its inverse does not. `loop-winding.gandr`"
534..603 Comment "// and `loop-space.gandr` count the words into the integers and back."
605..676 Comment "/// The loop\'s words as a presented type: its rules rewrite constructor"
677..731 Comment "/// terms, so a word normalizes to the loops it winds."
